{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/913259-can-a-kindred-join-any-blood-line","id":913259,"title":"Can a Kindred Join any Blood Line ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-12T23:18:28-07:00","id":913259,"title":"Can a Kindred Join any Blood Line ?","content":"I wanted to know can a kindred join any bloodline ?<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Kindred may join bloodlines as allowed by their Blood</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Potency dots. A character may join her sire\u2019s bloodline at Blood</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Potency 1. At Blood Potency 2, a vampire with which she shares</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">a blood tie </span></span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"color:#681d00\">(see p. 98) </span></span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">may act as Avus. At Blood Potency 4, any</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">vampire of her clan may act as an Avus. &quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Does this mean that as long as you have a blood tie you can join bloodlines of different clans ?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T23:59:51-07:00","id":913270,"title":"","content":"How do you propose to have blood ties to vampires of different clans? They're based on sirings.<br /> <br /> Most bloodlines are restricted by clan. There are a small handful of exception cases. The Neglatu cross clan boundaries because they are a bloodline of former clanless revenants; the Licinii are a curious blend of the blood of Nosferatu and of the dead Clan Julii; the wicked Twice-Dead are able to induct Kindred of any clan, though they treat their initiation as much as a punishment as a reward.<br /> <br /> What happens if a vampire uses blood ties forged across clan by the Mysteries of the Dragon or some esoteric Discipline to pledge to a bloodline? You've got yourself a plot hook, brother. Probably not a standard initiation, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T00:15:10-07:00","id":913276,"title":"","content":"There is the Kissing Cousins Devotion from the Secrets of the Covenant easter egg they linked a ways back. Still, as awesome as Daeva Kerberos (for example) would be, I doubt that is what the writer of either the B&amp;S section on bloodlines or the person behind the Kissing Cousins Devotion intended.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, even with that Devotion, I think you can't form more than a four stages removed blood sympathy between kindred of different clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 06-13-2016, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T00:20:43-07:00","id":913280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/913259-can-a-kindred-join-any-blood-line?p=913270#post913270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you propose to have blood ties to vampires of different clans? They're based on sirings.<br /> <br /> Most bloodlines are restricted by clan. There are a small handful of exception cases. The Neglatu cross clan boundaries because they are a bloodline of former clanless revenants; the Licinii are a curious blend of the blood of Nosferatu and of the dead Clan Julii; the wicked Twice-Dead are able to induct Kindred of any clan, though they treat their initiation as much as a punishment as a reward.<br /> <br /> What happens if a vampire uses blood ties forged across clan by the Mysteries of the Dragon or some esoteric Discipline to pledge to a bloodline? You've got yourself a plot hook, brother. Probably not a standard initiation, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought you could make a blood tie through blood sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T00:50:25-07:00","id":913288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/913259-can-a-kindred-join-any-blood-line?p=913280#post913280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I thought you could make a blood tie through blood sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other way around: blood sympathy (the act of sensing the status of cosanguinous Kindred) is made possible by having blood ties (cosanguinity) with your fellow Kindred. Blood ties are all based on branching lineages of the Embrace, meaning any blood tie not artificially created by blood sorcery or something is either within the same clan or pertains to some particular anomaly of the Blood.<br /> <br /> If you're looking at the passage on spending Willpower to force sympathy, that's not creating ties, that's intentionally sensing the status of a vampire with whom you have ties outside of the extreme situations that would spontaneously evoke your sympathetic senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 06-13-2016, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T01:31:39-07:00","id":913297,"title":"","content":"So wait you can't create a blood sympathy with a kindred out of your clan ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T02:56:39-07:00","id":913328,"title":"","content":"Not usually. Ghouls can sometimes develop it towards their regnant. Cruac and Theban establish a temporary link between the target of a ritual and the practitioner and there's a mystery that establishes it on vinculum bound subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T08:19:53-07:00","id":913391,"title":"","content":"In 2e it seems like you can create blood ties to anyone you want to by sharing your blood with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T08:56:19-07:00","id":913418,"title":"","content":"That's not mechanically the same as blood sympathy though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T10:54:51-07:00","id":913508,"title":"","content":"Are you confusing blood <b>ties</b> with the blood <b>bond?</b> The blood bond is the three-stage artificial infatuation characters develop when they drink a vampire's blood. It has nothing to do with blood ties or blood sympathy (outside of that one Mystery of the Dragon mentioned). Blood ties normally aren't something you create, they're a consequence of your siring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T11:00:46-07:00","id":913515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/913259-can-a-kindred-join-any-blood-line?p=913391#post913391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2e it seems like you can create blood ties to anyone you want to by sharing your blood with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you have the second dot of the Coil of the Voivode","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-13-2016, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}